1. Definitions

"Licensed Work" means the Trustalo software project and all source code,
build artifacts, configuration, and documentation in this repository.

"Production Use" means use of the Licensed Work in any live environment that
serves internal or external users, customers, or business operations.

"Qualified Organization" means an organization that has BOTH:
  a) annual gross revenue below USD 1,000,000; and
  b) total external funding raised below USD 1,000,000.

"Commercial License" means a separate written license agreement granted by the
Licensor that explicitly permits Production Use by organizations that are not
Qualified Organizations.

2. License Grant

Subject to this License, you may use, copy, modify, and create derivative
works of the Licensed Work for development, testing, evaluation, and other
non-production purposes.

Production Use is permitted only for Qualified Organizations.

3. Commercial Trigger

If an organization meets or exceeds either threshold below, it is not a
Qualified Organization and must obtain a Commercial License before any
Production Use:
  a) annual gross revenue of USD 1,000,000 or more; or
  b) total external funding raised of USD 1,000,000 or more.

4. Redistribution

You may redistribute source copies of the Licensed Work, with or without
modification, provided that:
  a) this License is included in full; and
  b) all copyright and attribution notices are preserved.

Redistribution does not grant recipients any rights beyond those stated in
this License.

5. Restrictions

Except as expressly permitted by this License, you may not:
  a) use the Licensed Work in Production Use if you are not a Qualified
     Organization and do not hold a Commercial License;
  b) represent this License as an open source license approved by OSI;
  c) use Licensor names, logos, or trademarks except for factual attribution.

6. Termination

Any use of the Licensed Work in violation of this License automatically
terminates your rights under this License.

